{"Title":"An Act establishing time limits for idling trains","BillNumber":"H3268","DocketNumber":"HD453","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J_B1","Name":"John Barrett, III","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/J_B1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T10:17:10.84"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"J_B1","Name":"John Barrett, III","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/J_B1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T10:17:10.84"},{"Id":"WSP1","Name":"Smitty Pignatelli","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WSP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-24T11:46:49.7433333"},{"Id":"CAF1","Name":"Carole A. Fiola","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CAF1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-09T15:31:34.0166667"},{"Id":"RME1","Name":"Rodney M. Elliott","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RME1","ResponseDate":"2023-06-22T13:46:58.55"},{"Id":"M_C1","Name":"Mike Connolly","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/M_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-06-26T09:54:45.1333333"},{"Id":"NJO1","Name":"Norman J. Orrall","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/NJO1","ResponseDate":"2023-06-26T13:28:36.6566667"},{"Id":"RMH2","Name":"Ryan M. Hamilton","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RMH2","ResponseDate":"2023-06-27T09:30:28.8533333"},{"Id":"TTN1","Name":"Tram T. Nguyen","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/TTN1","ResponseDate":"2023-06-28T11:24:15.1366667"},{"Id":"L_S1","Name":"Lindsay N. Sabadosa","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L_S1","ResponseDate":"2023-06-28T10:39:20.3033333"},{"Id":"M_C2","Name":"Michelle L. Ciccolo","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/M_C2","ResponseDate":"2023-06-28T11:50:16.63"},{"Id":"SWG1","Name":"Susan Williams Gifford","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SWG1","ResponseDate":"2023-06-28T15:29:27.87"},{"Id":"BWM1","Name":"Brian W. Murray","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BWM1","ResponseDate":"2023-06-30T19:54:23.75"},{"Id":"R_C1","Name":"Rob Consalvo","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/R_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-07-03T09:35:00.7866667"},{"Id":"SND0","Name":"Sal N. DiDomenico","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SND0","ResponseDate":"2023-07-12T16:20:32.93"},{"Id":"DAL1","Name":"David Henry Argosky LeBoeuf","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DAL1","ResponseDate":"2023-08-03T12:14:00.67"},{"Id":"J_A1","Name":"James Arciero","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/J_A1","ResponseDate":"2023-08-03T12:14:00.67"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3268/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Barrett of North Adams, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3268) of John Barrett, III, Smitty Pignatelli and Carole A. Fiola for legislation to establish idling time limits for trains.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tChapter 21A of the General Laws is hereby amended by adding the following section:-\r\n\tSection 28. No person shall cause, suffer, allow or permit a locomotive train engine to idle longer than 30 minutes. The department of environmental protection shall investigate all reported cases of train idling in excess of 30 minutes.  During its investigation, the department shall conduct emission tests to determine the level of carbon dioxide, nitrogen oxides, carbon monoxides, and sulfur dioxide being released from the train.\r\n\tEmission levels shall not exceed those of Massachusetts Bay Transportation Authority trains as previously determined by the United States Environmental Protection Agency.  If it is determined that these emission levels have been exceeded, the violator shall be fined no less than $5,000 for each violation.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}